s from s11-pending-dialog.md for Q5. Its delete-and-complete choice is required by TFA-92595 AC 8, so it is not judged as a bulk delete until Q5 is answered (S29 exercises it).","status":"skipped","steps":[],"parameters":[],"start":1791939095667,"stop":1791939095667,"duration":0,"type":"step","message":"Not automated in this run: a person checks it.","hasSimilarErrorInSubSteps":false},{"link":{"used":true,"missed":false,"id":"99c1a8787a521df83d16e93c75b04e6f","originalFileName":"7df98c11-25aa-43d7-9f17-427c2df4b8e6-attachment.txt","ext":".txt","contentType":"text/plain","contentLength":1943,"name":"agent's notes (facts it saw, not a verdict)"},"type":"attachment"},{"link":{"id":"a9a588aadd5dd680772c4a0d8c5dfb3b","originalFileName":"c7ec18c1-dfdd-4883-bd4a-a1c22fbc51e0-attachment.json","ext":".json","name":"oracle verdict","contentType":"application/json","used":true,"missed":false,"contentLength":3642},"type":"attachment"}],"error":{"message":"Checked by Quinn's runner (ledger.md #60): Blocked/Fail → case fix — Pending Tasks dialog has no accessible name (like Quick Dictation, U05) → check re-anchored (TC-24 + TC-17); settings checkpoint was saved while 'Loading…' (oracle Blocked it, as designed). Re-run below\nChecked by Quinn's runner (ledger.md #60b): Pass — no 'delete all patients' path on any screen (settings, lists, quick dictation, inbox, handoff, chart tabs, Pending Tasks dialog, NH lists/tasks)"},"testCase":{"id":"5e5f381d342d895fec16fbb8df7f1b8a","externalId":"651e8b3d410d028955500d7c80535e14","name":"[dev] S11 Bulk-delete hunt: no 'delete all' or similar control on any screen, in both modes","fullName":"TC-24 Deletions › TC-24/S11"},"descriptionHtml":"<p><b>Case priority: P0 · stated in the UAT / ticket AC</b> · UAT TC-24 ER 6; TFA-94700 AC 5 · “Each delete asks for confirmation once. No bulk delete.”.</p><div class=\"rc-approach\"><p><b>Approach</b> · TC-24 Deletions · <b>S11</b> Bulk-delete hunt: no 'delete all' or similar control on any screen, in both modes</p><p><b>UAT steps / ticket ACs covered:</b></p><ul><li><b>U9</b> No bulk delete anywhere in the app: records are deleted one at a time, and there is no 'delete all patients' or similar control. (UAT TC-24; TFA-92579 AC 2; TFA-94700 AC 5; TFA-94699 AC 6)</li><li><b>U10</b> Every TC-24 rule holds in both Hospital and Nursing Home, including deleting a Nursing Home resident. (UAT 3.3; UAT TC-24)</li></ul><p><b>Test design technique: </b>Error guessing (error-guessing) — Go straight for the places most likely to break (failures, double clicks, two tabs, a wrong clock, injected instructions).</p><p><b>Given </b>Hospital patient with two pending tasks and status note-ready; Nursing Home resident</p><p><b>When </b>Walk Settings, the Hospital list, Quick Dictation, Inbox, Handoff, the chart's Pre-Round and Encounter tabs, the Pending Tasks dialog on Post-Round (press 'Cancel — go back'), Nursing Home Today and All Residents, and the Nursing Home Tasks / Task Export screen</p><p><b>Then </b>No control deletes more than one record at once. The Pending Tasks dialog's choices are recorded for Q5, not judged.</p><p><b>Pass rule (oracle, excerpt): </b>TFA-94700 AC 5 'no ... bulk delete ... options appear anywhere' + UAT TC-24 'No bulk delete' + TFA-92579 AC 2. oracle.mjs mustNotContain per checkpoint ('Delete all', 'Remove all', 'Clear all', 'Delete selected', 'Clear completed', 'Discharge all'). …</p><p><b>Where it ran: </b>dev unit U60; test method AGENT · Browser agent; lane planned in the matrix: browser agent (automated)</p><p><small>S11 is our own case number (its number in the coverage matrix cases/TC-24.matrix.json), not a step number of the UAT document.</small></p></div><p><b>Environment: dev</b> — dev deployment, build <code>8b4be94</code> (Deploy Convex, 2026-10-19T17:04:37Z); account and address are not written into the report; run folder <code>runs/2026-10-14-dev</code>.</p><p><b>Test method:</b> AGENT · Browser agent; secondary: CODEREVIEW · Code review — as classified in cases/test-methods.json, which says it runs on both; Source: <code>dev</code>.</p><p><b>UAT item:</b> TC-24 Deletions · <b>Section:</b> A5 · Cross-Cutting · <b>Scenario:</b> TC-24/S11</p><p><b>Bulk-delete hunt: no 'delete all' or similar control on any screen, in both modes</b></p><p><b>Tickets:</b> TFA-92579 Home Screen: Patient Chart Card (ready for qa); TFA-94699 Data Retention &amp; Purge (in progress); TFA-94700 Physician Settings &amp; AI Consent (store requirements) (ready for qa)</p><p><b>Result:</b> Pass from <code>scripts/oracle.mjs</code> on the saved evidence (<code>units/U60.verdict.json</code>), unit U60. Agent: 60 turns, 150 s, $0.43.</p><p><b>Recorded (evidence only):</b></p><ul><li>s11-pending-dialog.md: (Q5: the dialog's delete-and-complete choice (required by TFA-92595 AC 8) is recorded, not judged as a bulk delete) pass: &quot;Delete Pending Tasks &amp; Complete&quot; present</li><li>s11-pending-dialog.md: (Q5: the dialog's other choices are recorded) pass: &quot;Keep Tasks &amp; Mark Complete&quot; present</li><li>(backend): (run sanity: 'Cancel — go back' kept both pending tasks (the agent pressed no delete)) pass: backend hosp-after tasks has 2 items</li><li>(backend): (run sanity: the encounter was not marked complete) pass: backend hosp-after status = &quot;note-ready&quot;</li></ul><p><b>Plan:</b> unit U60 (#50, rest, ui-only) — No bulk-delete control anywhere. Own seed; read-only sweep; tier 2 (TFA-94699 in its sources).</p><p><b>Checked by Quinn's runner</b> (<code>ledger.md</code> #60, U60; checked: yes): <b>Blocked/Fail → case fix</b> — Pending Tasks dialog has no accessible name (like Quick Dictation, U05) → check re-anchored (TC-24 + TC-17); settings checkpoint was saved while 'Loading…' (oracle Blocked it, as designed). Re-run below</p><p><b>Checked by Quinn's runner</b> (<code>ledger.md</code> #60b; checked: yes): <b>Pass</b> — no 'delete all patients' path on any screen (settings, lists, quick dictation, inbox, hand